<!--
  THE POSITIVE CONTROL. Byte-for-byte `attack-undefined-entity-no-doctype.xml` with the
  one undefined entity replaced by `&amp;`, which IS defined.

  Why a whole fixture for this: mutation testing against seven wrapper variants showed a
  wrapper whose `parseDocument` ALWAYS THREW passed every one of the ADR's three original
  assertions (SR-H-1). A suite made only of "this input raises" cases cannot tell a
  hardened port from a broken one. This file is the input that must SUCCEED, and it must
  produce a specific value — "Backend & Dev", not merely "something" — so a wrapper that
  returns an empty tree fails too.
-->
